# Eluge's flood counters may go on an opponent's lands ("target land"): as it enters and as it attacks, Bot1 floods
# Bot2's Mountains, which become Islands under Bot2 and tap for {U}. They are not Islands Bot1 controls, so Eluge stays
# a 2/2 for Bot1's two Islands and deals 2 (CR 604.3); and they are not lands Bot1 controls with flood counters, so
# Bot1's first instant, Opt, costs its full {U}. Nor does Eluge reduce Bot2's spells: Bot2's Mana Leak at the Opt,
# paid with the two flooded Mountains' {U}{U}, costs its full {1}{U}, so Bot2's pool is empty. Bot1 does not pay, and
# the Opt is countered.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Eluge, the Shoreless Sea
Opt
Island
Island
Island
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mountain
Mana Leak
Mountain x17

